@page "/developer"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Developer"; }
<h1>Developer</h1>
<p class="lead">Build applications with libpkg, connect to the portal, and share your packages.</p>
<div class="cards">
    <a class="card" href="/docs/dev-loop">
        <span class="eyebrow">Development loop</span>
        <span class="card-title">Build here, test on AROS</span>
        <span>Carry each build to an AROS machine as a signed package, know what it runs after a crash, roll back or repair, and let a script drive it.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/docs/self-update">
        <span class="eyebrow">libpkg integration</span>
        <span class="card-title">Update checks in your application</span>
        <span>Check compatible versions, read signed release notes and configure a channel in code or a .pkgupdate file.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/docs/reference#the-library">
        <span class="eyebrow">C API</span>
        <span class="card-title">Package operations with libpkg</span>
        <span>Install, browse and verify packages through the library, with progress, cancellation and structured results.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/developer/samples">
        <span class="eyebrow">Samples</span>
        <span class="card-title">Working examples</span>
        <span>C clients and a local HTTP demonstration with two signed builds.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/developer/api">
        <span class="eyebrow">Portal API</span>
        <span class="card-title">API and feeds</span>
        <span>Search packages, read metadata, subscribe to feeds and copy small or large badges.</span>
    </a>
</div>
